        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>EXAM FACT: Karnataka has the most Jnanpith Award winners (8) from any single language/state for Kannada.</strong></p><p>The award carries Rs. 11 lakh cash + Vagdevi (Saraswati) idol.</p><p>VK Gokak (1990) won for a Hindi epic poem — showing Karnataka writers' Hindi contributions too.</p><p>U.R. Ananthamurthy (1994) — his novel 'Samskara' was translated into 20+ languages.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
